codex
The false-result mutation built cleanly and failed at the intended obligation (`true` could not reach `false`), so the proof is non-vacuous. I also proved a bridge-free auxiliary claim using only the supplied semantics that loads the submitted `Module(FuncDef(...))`, resolves its real name binding, and calls it for arbitrary `N`; it closed with `#Top`. Changing the real body’s threshold from 8 to 9 then produced the expected stuck claim at `N=8`.
